{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{key: D}
{x_theme: faith-trust, grace-mercy}
{x_source: chrd:great_is_thy_faithfulness.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
[A]Great is Thy [D]faithfulness!
[Bm]Great is Thy [Em]faithfulness!
[A7]Morning by [D]morning new [E7]mercies I [A]see.
[A7]All I have [D]needed Thy [D]hand hath pro[Em]vided
[G]Great is Thy [D]faithfulness, [A]Lord [A7]unto  [D]me.

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Great is th[G]y faithfulness, [A7]O God my [D]Father,
[G]There is no [D]shadow of [E7]turning with [A]Thee;
[A7]Thou changest [D]not, Thy com[D]passions they [Em]fail not
[G]As Thou has [D]been Thou for[A]e -  [A7]ver wilt [D]be.

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Summer and [G]winter, and [A7]springtime and [D]harvest,
[G]Sun, moon, and [D]stars in their [E7]courses a[A]bove
[A7]Join with all [D]nature in [D]manifold [Em]witness
[G]To Thy great [D]faithfulness, [A]mer - [A7]cy and [D]love.

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Pardon for [G]sin and a [A7]peace that en[D]dureth,
[G]Thy own dear [D]presence to [E7]cheer and to [A]guide.
[A7]Strength for to[D]day and bright [D]hope for to[Em]morrow
[G]Blessings all [D]mine, with ten [A]thou-[A7]sand be[D]side.
